/-
  `SL(2, K)` is generated by its diagonal torus, its upper unipotent subgroup and
  the Weyl element `!![0, 1; -1, 0]`:

      `Subgroup.closure (diagonal ∪ unipotent ∪ {weyl}) = ⊤`.

  The port of the pin leaf

      `Matrix.SpecialLinearGroup.closure_diagonal_unipotent_weyl_eq_top`

  (`P2M/Sol/S_Matrix_SpecialLinearGroup_closure_diagonal_unipotent_weyl_eq_top.lean`
  — 86 pin lines; the pin's `S_` development is
  `namespace Matrix.SpecialLinearGroup.BruhatGeneration`, kept here under the pin's own
  `Matrix.SpecialLinearGroup` namespaces and its short names untouched), together with
  the statement of its `Theorems/` wrapper

      `Theorems/Thm_Matrix_SpecialLinearGroup_closure_diagonal_unipotent_weyl_eq_top.lean`.

  It is a faithful transcription: no statement is weakened, no route is generalised, and
  the pin's proofs are carried verbatim (`spec/check_port.py` diffs the single public
  declaration below against the two files named here).

  The mathematics is the Bruhat decomposition, in elementary form: `fin_two_induction`
  reduces an arbitrary `g = !![a, b; c, d]` to two cases. If `c = 0` then `a d = 1`, so
  `g = n(a b) · d(a)`; if `c ≠ 0` then
  `g = n(a / c) · d(-c⁻¹) · w · n(d / c)`. The generators are `dk a` (`diag(a, a⁻¹)`),
  `nk z` (the unipotent `!![1, z; 0, 1]`) and `wk` (`!![0, 1; -1, 0]`), and `genSet`
  is the pin's name for their union.

